    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Shale is one of the most complex rock types with a rich variety of failure structures. We present a synopsis of these structures first under two main categories: sharp and diffuse. Each of these categories has subclasses based on their displacement discontinuities including shear, compaction and dilation. We present examples for each class as well as complex structural assemblages that include more than one failure mode structure from various parts of the Globe and discuss their significance.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
